WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:13.858
Carefully, Vinnie and Mandy moved closer to the ship being tied to the dock.

2
00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:19.473
The Redcoat captain was speaking to a tall man in a black hat.

3
00:00:19.474 --> 00:00:27.644
He wore a long coat, pants that ended just below his knees, white stockings, and black shoes.

4
00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:39.746
"Mr. John Hancock," the captain read from a paper, "by order of His Royal Highness, King George III of England, you are under arrest."

5
00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:44.378
"What have I done?" John Hancock asked calmly.

6
00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:52.348
"Your ship, The Liberty, is carrying illegal tea into Boston Harbor," said the captain.

7
00:00:52.349 --> 00:00:58.096
Before John Hancock could say anything, the soldiers took him away.

8
00:00:58.097 --> 00:01:01.430
The men on the dock followed angrily.

9
00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:06.917
One of them saw Vinnie and Mandy and quickly walked over.

10
00:01:06.918 --> 00:01:11.501
"What are your names?" he asked when he got close.

11
00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:17.233
"I'm Vinnie, and this is my sister Mandy," said Vinnie bravely.

12
00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:21.466
"Are you American patriots?" the man asked.

13
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.999
"Yes, sir!" Vinnie said proudly.

14
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.679
"Good," the man said.

15
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.002
He took out a piece of paper and wrote something on it.

16
00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:35.870
"You must find John Adams and give this to him.

17
00:01:35.871 --> 00:01:40.166
Go quickly. No one will suspect you."

18
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:45.121
"Yes, sir." Vinnie saluted, but the man didn't see.

19
00:01:45.122 --> 00:01:49.258
He had already moved away to rejoin the others.

20
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:54.269
"Vinnie! Why did you say that?" Mandy said.

21
00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:57.840
"We don't even know who those men are!"

22
00:01:57.841 --> 00:02:02.368
"John Hancock? John Adams? Come on, Mandy.

23
00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:04.552
We are in Boston.

24
00:02:04.553 --> 00:02:09.673
These are the founders of our country!" Vinnie said passionately.

25
00:02:09.674 --> 00:02:13.542
"Right now, America is under British rule.

26
00:02:13.543 --> 00:02:15.907
We must help."

27
00:02:15.908 --> 00:02:19.761
"So what can we do?" she asked.

28
00:02:19.762 --> 00:02:26.690
"Just as the man said, we must find John Adams," explained Vinnie.

29
00:02:26.691 --> 00:02:31.094
The children walked down the busy Boston streets.

30
00:02:31.095 --> 00:02:35.712
Horses, carriages, and wagons were everywhere.

31
00:02:35.713 --> 00:02:39.168
Women were in simple cotton dresses.

32
00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:42.146
Men wore three-cornered hats.

33
00:02:42.147 --> 00:02:49.150
As they approached an intersection, Vinnie and Mandy heard shouting and clapping.

34
00:02:49.151 --> 00:02:52.963
"What's going on?" Vinnie wondered.

35
00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:59.313
On the next street, a crowd was gathered in front of a man standing on a barrel.

36
00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:02.198
He looked excited and angry.

37
00:03:02.199 --> 00:03:07.039
"Should we pay taxes to the British?" he shouted.

38
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.329
"No!" the crowd cheered.

39
00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.970
"We have no vote!

40
00:03:13.971 --> 00:03:19.080
We have no one to speak for us in England!" the man continued.

41
00:03:19.081 --> 00:03:22.061
People shouted loudly.

42
00:03:22.062 --> 00:03:25.467
"The Redcoats take over our homes!

43
00:03:25.468 --> 00:03:28.801
We pay too much for our tea!

44
00:03:28.802 --> 00:03:34.317
We even pay too much to mail our letters!" cried the man.

45
00:03:34.318 --> 00:03:39.725
"Who is he?" Mandy asked a boy standing nearby.

46
00:03:39.726 --> 00:03:44.015
"That's Mr. Keith, the grocer," said the boy.

47
00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:47.535
"Why is he shouting?" asked Vinnie.

48
00:03:47.536 --> 00:03:50.212
The boy stared at them.

49
00:03:50.213 --> 00:03:54.598
"You aren't from Boston, are you?" he said.

50
00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:57.728
"King George signed the Stamp Act.

51
00:03:57.729 --> 00:04:03.146
The law makes us pay extra money, a tax, for everything we buy.

52
00:04:03.147 --> 00:04:06.638
Everyone is very angry about it."

53
00:04:06.639 --> 00:04:18.256
"I never knew America was like this once," Mandy whispered to Vinnie.
